<title>UK: Halifax float worth up to 12 bln pounds.</title>
<headline>Halifax float worth up to 12 bln pounds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Halifax Building Society, Britain's largest mortgage lender, said on Friday its proposed June stock market flotation will be worth up to 12 billion pounds at a pricing of between 390 and 450 pence per share.</p>
<p>The society, with assets of over 100 billion pounds, said each qualifying member will receive a basic allocation of 200 shares in a flotation of 2.675 billion shares.</p>
</text>
